      <div type="clause" n="8.6">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 8.6</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 8.6" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="554" ed="#liebermann"/>Set de hiis omnibus pleniorem suggerent<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Hn_8-6.lnote.oe.27"/> uentura<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="k" target="#Hn_8-6.lnote.oe.k"/> noticiam, sicut Edwardi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="l" target="#Hn_8-6.lnote.oe.l"/> beatissimi principis extitisse temporibus<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Hn_8-6.lnote.oe.28"/> certis indiciis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Hn_8-6.lnote.oe.29"/> et fida relatione cognouimus.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 554 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_8-6.lnote.oe.k" n="k" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">554</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 41, 7 <hi rend="italic">ff.</hi> 65, 4</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. 41, 7 ff. 65, 4</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_8-6.lnote.oe.l" n="l" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">554</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Rechtszustand (Verfassung) Eadwards III. identificirt Verf. mit dem Staatsideal Heinrichs I.; offenbar hat er von jenem weder eigene Erinnerung noch kennt er das Rechtsbuch</hi> E Cf.</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">the author identifies the legal order (constitution) of Eadward III with the political ideal of Henry I; evidently he has no personal recollection of the former, nor does he know the law-book E Cf.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_8-6.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">554</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-rem <hi rend="italic">Lond;</hi> -runt <hi rend="italic">Sc Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-rem Lond; -runt Sc Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_8-6.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">554</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ris <hi rend="italic">Sc Hg</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ris Sc Hg</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_8-6.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">554</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">iud. <hi rend="italic">Co Or</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">iud. Co Or</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_8-6.lnote.oe._" n="-" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">317</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Set de his o. p. suggerem</hi>{27} <hi rend="italic">u. n. s. Eadw</hi>. Rs.—Es sind Stücke Cnuts, auf die Hn verweist: mit jenem identifiziert er Eadwardi (<hi rend="italic">s. d. Gl</hi> 8c) laga auch sonst.—8, 7 <hi rend="italic">docuerunt</hi>{31}—<hi rend="italic">circumpos</hi>.{33} besser? Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Set de his o. p. suggerem</hi>{27} <hi rend="italic">u. n. s. Eadw</hi>. Rs.—The passages to which Hn refers are Cnut’s: he identifies Eadwardi (<hi rend="italic">see</hi> that word in <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> 8c) laga with Cnut elsewhere too.—8, 7 <hi rend="italic">docuerunt</hi>{31}—<hi rend="italic">circumpos</hi>.{33} better? Rs</seg></note>
      </div>
